  "claims": {
    "path_laws": "ExchangeCoherence embeds existing bounded higher cells plus self contraction and adds structural groupoid laws. Explicit prefix/suffix cancellation cells are constructed; existence of a higher comparison is equivalent before/after appending a common path.",
    "extraction": "exposeHead scans until the first equal label, checking independence before crossing each preceding operation. It returns a residual word and an explicit Exchange path. Success iff some Exchange path exposes the chosen label.",
    "cancellation": "Erasing the first occurrence of any label preserves Exchange reachability. A common head can therefore be cancelled at the level of endpoint reachability.",
    "decision": "alignExchange recursively exposes successive target heads. Success iff Nonempty (Exchange signature one two), for all finite words, including repeated IDs, inverses and compositions. A successful result is an explicit path, without enumerating exchange paths.",
    "semantics": "Generated paths preserve the entire store distribution, uniformly in all typed local PMF kernels and every initial store.",
    "negative": "For read/write signature 0 reads {2} and writes {0}, 1 reads empty and writes {1}, 2 reads empty and writes {2}, descending swaps from [2,1,0] yield [1,2,0] and [2,0,1]. Both have no descending successors, are unequal, and have no common descending descendant. Thus this orientation is not locally confluent.",
    "recovery": "The complete generator connects those two descending terminals using two checked swaps, and rejects [2,1,0] to [0,1,2]."
  },
  "runtime_checks": [
    {
      "mechanism": "#guard_msgs in #eval",
      "expected": "([[1, 2, 0], [2, 0, 1]], [], [], true, false)",
      "meaning": "Successors of the peak; successors of each terminal; exposing 1 succeeds from [2,0,1]; exposing 0 fails from [2,1,0].",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "mechanism": "#guard_msgs in #eval",
      "expected": "(true, false, 2)",
      "meaning": "Terminal alignment accepted; dependency-violating order rejected; generated terminal alignment uses two primitive swaps.",
      "passed": true
    }
  ],
  "scope": [
    "Completeness concerns the generated checked-exchange syntax, not all semantically equal probabilistic programs or arbitrary cryptographic transformations.",
    "Target-directed alignment is not a proof of canonical normalization or global higher coherence. An explicit comparison between arbitrary parallel paths is still required.",
    "The structural groupoid laws are explicit new higher constructors. They are not claimed derived from the former three root forms or to form a complete finite presentation.",
    "The descending-swap counterexample refutes this chosen orientation only; it does not refute other normalization strategies or finite higher presentations.",
    "No new copy/discard, approximate game, dynamic scheduling, native CPU-time, proof-DAG size, byte-size or checking-time bound is established.",
    "No actual MAC execution or interface changed. Earlier full caller/cache/trace results retain their inputs.",
    "The two-swap count is a primitive-rule count for this diagnostic example, not an exclusive higher-dimensional advantage."
  ],
